---
import ContentLayout from "astro-theme-university/layouts/ContentLayout.astro";
import SessionsGrid from "../../components/SessionsGrid.astro";
import { sessionLabels, siteConfig } from "../../site-config";
---

<ContentLayout
  title={sessionLabels.plural}
  description="One technique, many programs. What happens in the room each week, what to bring, and why it is not your assignment."
  {...siteConfig}
>
  <p>
    Each session takes the week's technique and applies it to a program chosen
    for the purpose. <strong>You are encouraged to use your own assignment
    target where it suits</strong> — some weeks it will, some weeks it will be
    the wrong shape entirely — and every session offers suggestions so nobody
    spends the hour deciding what to work on.
  </p>
  <p>
    That decoupling is deliberate. Your assignment is one program against many
    techniques, which gives you depth. A session is one technique against many
    programs, which is the only way the room finds out where that technique
    actually stops. If everyone brought their own target every week we would
    get twenty shallow passes instead of a map.
  </p>
  <p>
    Sessions are not marked and do not build toward the assignments. Bring a
    laptop and something you are prepared to be wrong about.
  </p>
  <SessionsGrid />
</ContentLayout>
